*  earn0_varref_bare_dropped.sno - PATTERN-VALUED VAR DROPPED IN A STORED PATTERN (2026-08-12 s29).
*  THE SMALLEST MEMBER OF THE CLASS: a bare stored reference, no concatenation at all.
*  P is a PATTERN. Q = P stores it. Matching '' (null subject) against Q must FAIL,
*  because LEN(1) cannot match a null subject.
*  AT HEAD fc5b0754 SCRIP PRINTS 'MATCH' WITH rc=0 -- Q behaves as the NULL PATTERN,
*  i.e. the pattern-valued variable was read as null.
*  SUBJECT CHOSEN TO DISCRIMINATE: with a non-null subject BOTH the correct and the
*  defective compiler print MATCH, so the obvious test is VACUOUS. Do not "simplify"
*  this witness by changing the subject -- that is what hid the defect (RULES: a control
*  whose arms predict the same output is not a control).
*  ⭐ s29 KILLSWITCH A/B: SCRIP_PAT_INLINE=0 REPAIRS this witness outright (FAIL->PASS).
*  That convicts DEFECT A: LOWER elides the pattern-valued ASSIGN in favour of use-site
*  inlining, and a use inside another stored pattern is not an inlining site.
*  ⛔ The knob is a DIAGNOSTIC DISCRIMINATOR, never a fix and never a revert path.
        P = LEN(1)
        Q = P
        '' Q                                     :S(Y)F(N)
Y       OUTPUT = 'MATCH'                         :(D)
N       OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH'
D       OUTPUT = 'DONE'
END
